<h1>A short guide</h1>
<p>Lume reads like Python and runs like Rust. Start with <code>def main:</code>.</p>
<h2>Values</h2>
<p>Everything is a value: <code>1</code>, <code>&quot;text&quot;</code>, <code>[1, 2]</code>, <code>{&quot;a&quot;: 1}</code>, <code>{1, 2}</code>. A value that may be absent has type <code>T?</code>, and one that may fail is <code>T or Error</code>.</p>
<h2>Blocks</h2>
<pre><code>xs.map { |x| x * 2 }
xs.each do |x|
  puts x</code></pre>
<p>That is the whole of it. See the <a href="index.html">front page</a>.</p>
</main>
